---
name: transcribe-gas-bill
description: Transcribe a landed gas bill PDF into a gas_bill_record, check it and land it. Use when the owner asks to add a gas bill, or a gas bill PDF waits in data/landing/.
---

# transcribe-gas-bill

Use the `energatron` MCP tools when this session has them (`tool_name` below); otherwise run the same command with
`uv run energatron <command> --json` from this folder. Identifiers (account, MIRN, invoice, reference and meter
numbers, the address) stay out of the record: it has no field for them. Never copy anything from the bill elsewhere.

1. **Land the PDF** if it isn't yet: `land_file` with `source: gas_bill` and `dry_run: true` (`energatron land
   data/landing/<bill>.pdf --source gas_bill --dry-run`), then without. Note its dataset ID (`gas_bill-…`).
2. **Read the bill**: `read_gas_bill_text` (offered only when the owner started the server with `--allow-documents`;
   `energatron gas-bill text <ID>`), or ask the owner for the figures.
3. **Fill the record** (`new_gas_bill_record` / `energatron gas-bill new <ID> --extracted-by agent:<your model id>`
   writes a commented skeleton): `kind: gas_bill_record`, `schema_version: 2`, `extracted_by: agent:<your model id>`
   (`manual` when the owner typed it); the retailer and plan as printed; `issue_date`, `period_start`, `period_end`
   as quoted `YYYY-MM-DD` (the period is inclusive); one `reads` entry per printed read, oldest first (date, `actual`
   or `estimate`, start and end index, heating value, pressure factor, MJ as printed); `lines` for this period's
   charges only, GST-exclusive as printed (a `usage` line per usage step in MJ x $/MJ, a `supply` line per supply rate
   in days x $/day, discounts and credits negative, `gst_free: true` for anything applied after GST; convert c/MJ to
   $/MJ); `subtotal` (before GST), `gst`, `total` (this period's charges including GST, never a carried balance).
   Every number and date is a quoted string.
4. **Check** it: `check_gas_bill_record` (`energatron gas-bill check <file>`). Every check must pass; a failing check
   is a transcription error: compare with the bill and fix it. Never adjust a figure just to make a check pass.
5. **Write** it: `write_gas_bill_record` (`energatron gas-bill write <file>`): it runs the same checks and writes the
   record into `data/landing/`. Then `land_file` that path (dry run first).
6. **Run** `run_pipeline` (`energatron run`); every `gas_bills` check must pass. A corrected record lands as a new
   dataset; the newest per PDF wins.
7. **Tariff in force** (once per plan): if the bill's plan isn't a landed offer, tell the owner the backtest needs an
   `offer_manual` for it. Then `status`: a backup is pending.
